      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Setting up the SkyLink CLI correctly ensures immediate productivity for your engineering team by guaranteeing a standardized toolchain across all project repositories. Before initiating any installations, verify that your local Docker daemon is active and accessible, as SkyLink relies entirely on Docker Compose or containerized services for orchestration and background processing tasks. You must also confirm that your system supports Node.js version 18 or higher, since the CLI binary includes native bindings and cryptographic libraries designed specifically for this runtime version to prevent runtime errors during package resolution. Install the global tool using the command `npm install -g skylink-cli`, which pulls the latest production-ready binaries from our secure repository and registers them permanently within your system's PATH for universal accessibility. This tool facilitates seamless integration with our internal CI/CD pipelines, so ensuring it is up to date is crucial for compatibility with future version rolls. After installation, execute `skylink login` to generate a secure OAuth token that authenticates your local workstation to the central SkyLink configuration server and repository backend. This step is non-negotiable, as it maps your project roots to your specific access keys and ensures your changes are routed to your designated team queues within the cloud infrastructure. Finally, deploy your application by running `skylink",
      "source": "target",
